ling artifact: the isolated bench's\n        # real-weight loader only ever sees layer 0, the 314k outlier.  Most QKV\n        # layers have ~1.6k exceptions and fuse-win.)\n        # best-N re-derived by an 8-step N sweep on a representative (median-exc)\n        # real layer (layer 40, N=8..256, H2D).  Cliff is structural: at N>64 the\n        # small-M shapes (QKV/O/Down) remap to the slow Npad=192 WGMMA tile\n        # (_pad_n), so they lose past 64; GateUp's large M keeps a clean Npad=128\n        # and keeps winning to 128.  Ratios @best-N: QKV 1.12x, O 1.09x, GateUp\n        # 1.20x@128, Down 1.49x.\n        (10240, 8192): 64,    # QKV    (wins N<=64 ~1.12x; N>=96 -> Npad=192 cliff)\n        (8192, 8192): 128,    # O      (serving batch-128: avoid dense WDecomp)\n        (57344, 8192): 128,   # GateUp (was 64; wins to 128, big M -> Npad=128)\n        (8192, 28672): 128,   # Down   (serving batch-128: avoid dense WDecomp)\n    }\n\n    def _fused_max_n_for(self, M: int, K: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Per-layer fused N threshold (0 = never fuse this shape); unknown\n        shapes fall back to 128.  An instance-level ``_fused_max_n_override``\n        (set by tests/benchmarks) overrides all shapes.\n        \"\"\"\n        if self._fused_max_n_override is not None:\n            return self._fused_max_n_override\n        return self._FUSED_MAX_N_TABLE.get((M, K), 128)\n\n    def linear_apply(self, comp, x, wdecomp_events=None):\n        \"\"\"Fused decode + GEMM forward: y = x @ W^T, x [..., K] -> [..., M].\n\n        Uses the P4-RS register-A WGMMA kernel for decode-N (N <=\n        ``_fused_max_n``); falls back to decompress + ``F.linear`` for large N\n        (prefill) or non-aligned shapes. The codec's GPU-resident buffers live\n        on ``comp._c`` (kept current by both ``.to()`` and ``build_split_shell``).\n\n        ``wdecomp_events`` = optional ``(begin, end)`` external events bracketing\n        ONLY the fallback ``decompress`` so --time-breakdown WDe